`++`/`--` inside a larger expression (diag.increment_as_statement): info
for a single use, warning when the same statement uses the variable again,
since operands evaluate left to right and each increment lands before the
next is read. Whole-statement increments stay silent (issue #347).
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE Walk;
	:PARAMETERS aRows;
	:DECLARE nIndex, vItem, aSeen, nSum;
	nIndex := 1;
	vItem := aRows[nIndex++];
	aSeen[nIndex++] := nIndex;
	nSum := nIndex++ + nIndex++;
	nIndex++;
	:RETURN vItem;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE Walk;
	:PARAMETERS aRows;
	:DECLARE nIndex, vItem, aSeen, nSum;

	nIndex := 1;
	vItem := aRows[nIndex++];
	aSeen[nIndex++] := nIndex;
	nSum := nIndex++ +nIndex++;
	nIndex++;

	:RETURN vItem;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
6:8-6:16 warning increment_as_statement: 'nIndex' is incremented and used again in the same expression - operands evaluate left to right and each '++' lands before the next is read; increment it in its own statement
7:10-7:18 warning increment_as_statement: 'nIndex' is incremented and used again in the same expression - operands evaluate left to right and each '++' lands before the next is read; increment it in its own statement
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
5:17-5:25 info increment_as_statement: '++' is used inside a larger expression - postfix yields the old value and prefix the new; write the increment as its own statement
6:8-6:16 warning increment_as_statement: 'nIndex' is incremented and used again in the same expression - operands evaluate left to right and each '++' lands before the next is read; increment it in its own statement
7:10-7:18 warning increment_as_statement: 'nIndex' is incremented and used again in the same expression - operands evaluate left to right and each '++' lands before the next is read; increment it in its own statement
